Issue #825: ruvector-delta-index test_insert_and_search hangs indefinitely (DeltaHnsw insert/search)

## Overview

`ruvector-delta-index::tests::test_insert_and_search` (`crates/ruvector-delta-index/src/lib.rs:731`) hangs indefinitely — it never terminates rather than being merely slow. It is not part of the cause of the current `Tests (core-and-rest)` 240-minute CI failures (see "Scope clarification" below), but it is a real defect that had the crate held out of CI.

## Failing test

```rust
fn random_vector(dim: usize) -> Vec<f32> {
    use rand::Rng;
    let mut rng = rand::thread_rng();
    (0..dim).map(|_| rng.gen()).collect()
}

#[test]
fn test_insert_and_search() {
    let mut index = DeltaHnsw::new(128, DeltaHnswConfig::default());
    for i in 0..100 {
        let vec = random_vector(128);
        index.insert(&format!("vec_{}", i), vec).unwrap();
    }
    assert_eq!(index.len(), 100);
    let query = random_vector(128);
    let results = index.search(&query, 10).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(results.len(), 10);
}
```

## Evidence

- Observed on CI run [31675583441](https://github.com/ruvnet/ruvector/actions/runs/31675583441) (PR #822, `ci/split-core-platform`): the `core-platform` shard sat in a nextest SLOW loop on this single test for **3h 52m** until the 240-minute job cap; no other test in the shard progressed after it started.
- The hang is almost certainly an unterminated loop in `DeltaHnsw::insert` or `DeltaHnsw::search` — a candidate-set/visited-set traversal that fails to make progress (e.g. a neighbor-list cycle, or a `while` over a candidate heap that re-pushes an already-visited node).

## Nondeterminism

The test input is built from unseeded `rand::thread_rng()`, so the hang only reproduces for graph topologies that trigger the bug — consistent with the test having passed on earlier runs before the shard split surfaced it.

## Scope clarification (from comments)

An earlier claim that this hang was "very likely the reason **every** PR shows a red `Tests (core-and-rest)`" was **retracted by its author**:

- `ruvector-delta-index` is explicitly excluded from both the `core-platform` and `core-and-rest` shard package sets in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (with comments citing this issue). A crate that never runs in a shard cannot hang it.
- In the cited job (97356253593 / 97231570606, Workspace run 32702332738), the job hit the 240-minute cap while Cargo was still compiling crates (`ruvector-temporal-tensor-wasm`, `ruvector-profiler`, `ruvector-dither`, etc.) — no DeltaHnsw test executed.
- The shard-truncation bug (a `#` inside a folded YAML scalar silently eating `--exclude` flags) was fixed on 2026-08-13 in `09cccfebe`; on current `main`, `core-and-rest` carries its full 162 excludes.
- PR #787 is a credible separate fix for the DeltaHnsw defect but is **not** the fix for the recurring `core-and-rest` 240-minute cancellations.

## Impact on CI

Until fixed, a hung test burns the full 240-minute job budget. Two mitigations landed in PR #822:

1. `.config/nextest.toml` sets `slow-timeout = { period = "120s", terminate-after = 5 }` — any test is killed and reported as failure after 10 minutes.
2. `ruvector-delta-index` is temporarily held out of CI entirely: removed from `core-platform`'s package list and kept in `core-and-rest`'s `--exclude` list.

## Fix checklist

- [ ] Root-cause the non-terminating loop in `DeltaHnsw::insert` / `DeltaHnsw::search`
- [ ] Add a progress/iteration bound so a malformed graph fails loudly instead of hanging
- [ ] Seed the test RNG (or use a fixed fixture) so the case is deterministic and regression-testable
- [ ] Re-add `-p ruvector-delta-index` to the `core-platform` shard and drop its `--exclude` from `core-and-rest` in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`

